  "title": "CJP Protest Over Election Commission Resignation in Delhi",
  "summary": "Opposition leaders and activists in Delhi, including Congress president Kharge and leaders from the Indian National Congress, have called for the immediate resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar to address allegations of electoral irregularities and voter rights. The protest, led by Abhijeet Dipke and other figures, highlights ongoing tensions between the government and the CJP.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The CJP staged a protest demanding the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar in Delhi in October.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Abhijeet Dipke, a key figure in the CJP, expressed concerns over the potential removal of 13 crore voters from electoral rolls.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The protest was organized with the aim of addressing political tensions and ensuring judicial oversight in the electoral process.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
